// FIELD SERVICE — TRUCK STOP — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// FIELD SERVICE as country and bluegrass — the field-service van pulled in off the highway
// and the truck stop's house band on. A game alternate of plumber, selectable from the dev
// menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Peter: "a bunch of remixes of cabinet songs that take advantage of the new guitar presets…
// something different." The FRPP-6 string band, at 132: the theme's sixteenths are a fiddle
// tune's eighths in cut time.
// 
//   TELE (frppElectricBridge) — the hook, chicken-picked: snapped sixteenths, sixths and thirds
//     double-stopped under it, muted clucks between (frppFunkMuted), slapback and spring
//   BANJO (frppBanjo, free strings) — the tune in Scruggs rolls; forward rolls behind the band
//   SLIDE (frppSlideGuitar) — the pedal steel's swells under the hook, a crying half-speed solo
//   FIDDLE (frppViolin, a quicker bow) — the C phrase, the hook an octave up, a break, twin harmony;
//     a second fiddle on double-stop drones
//   ACOUSTIC (frppSteelAcoustic, down-strums) — boom-chick, Lester Flatt G-runs
//   MANDOLIN (frppMandolin, muted) — the chop on 2 and 4
//   BASS (frppBassNeck) — upright two-beat, walking in the choruses
//   KIT — brushes on the train beat; sticks, a round kick and a tambourine in the last chorus
// 
// The harmony is the theme's, a chord a half bar — A | Am F | C G(sus4–3) |, B | Am C G | F G |,
// C | Am C G | Am C G |, the rising ending | Am | E7 | — every guitar chord an open shape.
// 
//    1–4   KICKOFF — the banjo alone with the tune in its rolls; the band at 3; a G-run, and the
//          slide diving through 4.4 (plumber-1's power-down beat) so the band lands on 5.1
//    5–12  HEAD — Tele on the hook, A A B B(rise); slide swells; banjo rolls + chop from the B
//   13–20  CHORUS — fiddle on the C phrase over plumber's own harmony (slide); then A A, the
//          band, the fiddle an octave over the Tele
//   21–36  BREAKS — BANJO (A A) · FIDDLE (B B, drone fiddle) · SLIDE (hook at half speed,
//          half-time) · TELE (chicken pickin', sixths, clucks, back to the hook)
//   37–40  CLIMB — stop-time on plumber's build figure over Esus4 | E7, the same up a whole step
//          (the truck-driver's gear change), the rising ending into B minor
//   41–56  LAST CHORUS in B minor — A A B B C C A A; sticks; Tele double-stops; fiddle 8va + twin
//   57–60  TAG — A minor again, the banjo's kickoff over the band, the dive into bar 5
// 
// The loop is bars 5–60; bars 1–4 loop on the cabinet screen. Levelled by solo measurement; the trailing gain -5.3 dB puts the song at -21.0 LUFS integrated (peak -1.1 dBFS).
// 60 bars at 132, 109 s. Written by work/local/_fs-remix-truck-stop.mjs
// through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
